					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2313679#post-2872435</guid>
				<title>Re: 173 Festival</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2313679/10-years-birthday-scparty#post-2872435</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 19 Jun 2017 14:12:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dexanote</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>481882</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <h2><span>AND THE INITIAL POSTING TIME FOR THIS CHALLENGE HAS PASSED - 10 DAYS, 10 HOURS, for 10 YEARS.</span></h2> <p>Every single Tale that was posted to this challenge <strong>before</strong> the end time has been provided with an absolutely <em><strong>fabulous</strong></em> banner, created by our best and only <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cyantreuse" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2303803&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1497881777" alt="Cyantreuse" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2303803)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cyantreuse" >Cyantreuse</a></span> just for the occasion! It's a gif - blink and you'll miss it. ;)</p> <p>I'll be retrofitting this Challenge hub in the next few days into something else, but still related to 173 - feel absolutely free to still write whatever you like, and if you happen to do something inspired by this about 173, totally tag it <strong>173fest</strong>! Just know that <span style="text-decoration: underline;">any entries posted after the timestamp on this comment are not currently eligible for the neato banner</span>. That's the rules!</p> <p>Thank you everyone for making this challenge a fantastic success, and I'm thrilled to see so many varied, short pieces of fiction about our favourite <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statues_(game)">playground game</a>. A couple are even first posts - that warms me deeply.</p> <p>I hope contributors here enjoyed the game, and I'm looking forward to re-reading (and reading) them all again.</p> <p>edited because formatting lmao</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
